      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a predictive model for residential property theft risk for our underwriting team. we're looking at changes in specific urban zip codes over the last 5 years. i have some data on demographic shifts and larceny rates. i need to know if there's a statistically significant correlation between increased ethnic diversity in these zones and the rise in theft incidents, or if we should be looking at other socioeconomic variables instead. can you help me analyze how much weight we should give to changes in ethnic composition in our risk profiles?",
